Ladybird gives a scroll container in a min-content grid column its
content’s min-content width, and gives it only its minimum width toward
an auto track sized under an intrinsic constraint. Chrome and Firefox
give the reduced case’s link the same 84px width. WebKit sets a
min-content track’s base size from GridTrackSizingAlgorithmStrategy::
minContentContributionForGridItem(), with no exception for scroll
containers, and Blink’s CalculateIntrinsicMinimumContribution() makes
only a scroll container’s automatic minimum size zero.
